### Logical Relationships

```
G1 -> G2, G3, G4, G5, G6, G7 [AND][(sequential)]
G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [AND][(parallel)]
G4 -> G4.1, G4.2 [OR][(parallel)]
G5.1 -> G5.1.1, G5.1.2, G5.1.3 [AND][(parallel)]
G6 -> G6.1, G6.2 [AND][(parallel)]
G7 -> G7.1, G7.2 [AND][(parallel)]

G4.1 -> AT4 [AND]
G4.2 -> AT5 [AND]
G3.1 -> AT2 [AND]
G3.2 -> AT3 [AND]
G5.1.1 -> AT10 [AND]
G5.1.2 -> AT11 [AND]
G5.1.3 -> AT12 [AND]
G6.1 -> AT9 [AND]
G6.2 -> AT8 [AND]
G7.1 -> AT6 [AND]
G7.2 -> AT7, AT13, AT14 [OR][(parallel)]
```

> **Note:**  
> * `;` denotes sequential execution of the top‑level steps.  
> * `-` indicates that no special runtime structure is required for that goal.  
> * OR decompositions allow the robot to succeed by completing any one of the child goals.  
> * The tasks are directly linked to their parent goals with an AND relation, ensuring that every required action is executed.
